  "body": {
    "cards": {
      "color": {
        "element": "water",
        "role": "yongsin",
        "text": {
          "evidence": [
            {
              "basis": {
                "segments": [
                  {
                    "text": "On a Day to go gently, we based your lucky color on the element that reconnects a blocked flow, and on other days on your "
                  },
                  {
                    "term": "role.yongsin",
                    "text": "Yongsin"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " element. Your lucky direction follows this base element as it is."
                  }
                ]
              },
              "detail": {
                "day_kind": "ORDINARY_DAY",
                "element": "WATER",
                "role": "YONGSIN"
              },
              "ruleId": "color/lucky_element",
              "source": {
                "segments": [
                  {
                    "text": "Each element has its true color: Water is black, Fire is red, Wood is blue-green, and Earth is yellow.\n推其形色，則水黑、火赤、木青、土黃，此正色也。及其變易，則不然。常以生旺從正色，死絶從母色，成形冠帶從妻色，病敗從鬼色，旺墓從子色。\nGungtong Bogam, 五行總論"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "sourceRef": "gungtong-bogam/five_elements#color"
            },
            {
              "basis": {
                "segments": [
                  {
                    "text": "The classics hold that an element's color changes with the stage it sits in that day. Today Water sits at Jangsaeng on the branch 申, so we chose black. Your direction doesn't change this way and follows the base element."
                  }
                ]
              },
              "detail": {
                "base_element": "WATER",
                "day_branch": "申",
                "element": "WATER",
                "shift": "JEONG",
                "twelve_stage": "JANGSAENG"
              },
              "ruleId": "color/shift",
              "source": {
                "segments": [
                  {
                    "text": "The true colors are black for water, red for fire, blue-green for wood, white for metal and yellow for earth, but when they change, growth and peak follow the true color, death and severance the color of the element that gives birth to it, formation and capping the color of the element it overcomes, sickness and decay the color of the element that overcomes it, and the tomb after the peak the color of the element it gives birth to.\n推其形色則水黑火赤木青金白土黃此正色也及其變易則不然常以生旺從正色死絶從母色成形冠帶從妻色病敗從鬼色旺墓從子色\nSammyeong Tonghoe, 論五行"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "sourceRef": "sammyeong-tonghoe/five_elements#color_change"
            }
          ],
          "messageKey": "color.ordinary_day",
          "reactable": false,
          "slot": "daily.color",
          "text": {
            "segments": [
              {
                "text": "Your chart needs Water energy, so black suits you today."
              }
            ]
          },
          "todayReason": {
            "segments": [
              {
                "text": "We chose the color of the energy that supports your chart."
              }
            ]
          },
          "variant": "single"
        }
      },
      "direction": {
        "direction": "nw",
        "text": {
          "evidence": [
            {
              "basis": {
                "segments": [
                  {
                    "text": "Since it's an Ordinary day, from the day's lucky directions we chose Northwest, which matches Metal, your "
                  },
                  {
                    "term": "role.huisin",
                    "text": "Huisin"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": " element."
                  }
                ]
              },
              "detail": {
                "day_branch": "申",
                "day_kind": "ORDINARY_DAY",
                "deity": "XI",
                "direction": "NW",
                "element": "METAL"
              },
              "ruleId": "direction/ordinary_deity_huisin",
              "source": {
                "segments": [
                  {
                    "text": "The north gives rise to Water, the south to Fire, the east to Wood, the west to Metal, and the center to Earth.\n北方陰極而生寒，寒生水。南方陽極而生熱，熱生火。東方陽散以泄而生風，風生木。西方陰止以收而生燥，燥生金。中央陰陽交而生溫，溫生土。其相生也所以相維，其相剋也所以相制，此之謂有倫。\nGungtong Bogam, 五行總論"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "sourceRef": "gungtong-bogam/five_elements#direction"
            }
          ],
          "messageKey": "direction.day_kind.ordinary.mo",
          "reactable": false,
          "slot": "daily.direction_relation",
          "text": {
            "segments": [
              {
                "text": "Head Northwest, the way of Metal, which generates the Water energy your chart needs."
              }
            ]
          },
          "todayReason": {
            "segments": [
              {
                "text": "Of the calendar's lucky directions, we chose the one of the energy that backs up your chart."
              }
            ]
          },
          "variant": "single"
        }
      },
