        "text": {
          "evidence": [
            {
              "basis": {
                "segments": [
                  {
                    "text": "We favored hours that support today's day pillar or join with it, and left out hours that clash with it."
                  }
                ]
              },
              "detail": {
                "day_pillar": "庚申",
                "hour_branch": "SHIN",
                "period": "DAY"
              },
              "ruleId": "focus_time/day_relation",
              "source": {
                "segments": [
                  {
                    "text": "The hour serves the day, so all that matters is whether it supports the day: if it shares the energy of the day stem or branch or forms a three-way or six-way union with the day branch, it is lucky, and rather than following every lucky and unlucky spirit of the hour, only Gwiin, Rok and Ma count as lucky.\n時者日之用也全在幇扶日辰或與日支干比和或與日支三合六合即吉時家吉凶神不必盡拘惟貴人祿馬為吉\nHyeopgi Byeonbangseo, 用時法"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "sourceRef": "xieji-bianfang/hours#use_hour"
            },
            {
              "basis": {
                "segments": [
                  {
                    "text": "We favored hours that support or join with the heavenly stem of your birth year, and avoided hours that clash with your birth year."
                  }
                ]
              },
              "detail": {
                "birth_year": "庚午",
                "hour_branch": "SHIN",
                "period": "DAY"
              },
              "ruleId": "focus_time/birth_year",
              "source": {
                "segments": [
                  {
                    "text": "People of old all looked at the heavenly stem of the birth year, choosing times that join with its officer or wealth, act as its peer or seal, sit at its growth stage, or bring its Rok, Ma and Gwiin, without clashing with or overcoming the birth chart.\n古人皆論生年之天干或合官或合財或比肩或印綬或四長生或取祿馬貴人不衝命尅命\nHyeopgi Byeonbangseo, 論相主"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "sourceRef": "xieji-bianfang/hours#birth_year"
            },
            {
              "basis": {
                "segments": [
                  {
                    "text": "We also checked whether the hour is one the classic almanac marks as a lucky Hwangdo hour."
                  }
                ]
              },
              "detail": {
                "hour_branch": "SHIN",
                "huangdao": "false",
                "period": "DAY"
              },
              "ruleId": "focus_time/huangdao",
              "source": {
                "segments": [
                  {
                    "text": "When counting hours from the day, on a Ja day Cheongnyong starts at the Sin hour and Myeongdang falls at the Yu hour, and the rest follow in order.\n日起時則子日申時起青龍酉時為明堂依次順數\nHyeopgi Byeonbangseo, 黃道黑道"
                  }
                ]
              },
              "sourceRef": "xieji-bianfang/hours#huangdao"
            }
          ],
          "messageKey": "focus_time.day",
          "reactable": false,
          "slot": "daily.focus_time",
          "text": {
            "segments": [
              {
                "text": "This is a good time for important things."
              }
            ]
          },
          "variant": "single"
        }
      },
